   "reply_text": "screenshot_gui REFUSED: this window is not rendering, so there is no frame to capture. A GUI screenshot is the one MCP call that needs a real rendered frame \u2014 it is taken by the render backend, not by a rasteriser. Last frame 8.5s ago; frame_loop.healthy is false and has been for at least 2s. This is not a timeout and retrying will not help. Mechanism: on Wayland a hidden, occluded or screen-locked surface receives no compositor frame callbacks, and under the FIFO present family the main thread can block inside the present itself. Remedies, in order: make the window visible; or relaunch with WAYLAND_DISPLAY unset so winit picks X11/XWayland; and check frame_loop.present_mode.negotiated \u2014 if it reads Fifo or FifoRelaxed the park hazard is in force. screenshot_simulation and screenshot_toolpath are CPU rasterisers and still work."
